tion_jobs`/`user_actions`/`critique_resolution_coverage` (clearance had 0 findings), and all objectives \\u2264240 chars with no semicolons.\\n\\nThe finalized plan is written to `finalize_output.json`. Summary of the DAG:\\n\\n- **Foundation chain:** T1 (port CL1 verbatim + golden) \\u2192 T2 (v2 schemas) \\u2192 {T3 semantic-loop, T4 migrations} \\u2192 T5 (store/append, c8 auto-split) \\u2192 T6 (replay, c7 auto-split) \\u2192 T7 (active-action) \\u2192 T8 (accountability)\\n- **Independent branches:** T12 (cancelled-archive audit, no deps \\u2014 runs early/parallel), T10 (importer, off T2+T5), T11 (freshness, off T2+T6)\\n- **Step 13 split into 3 independent test families:** T13a (negative-mutation), T13b (concurrency/crash), T13c (compat/privacy)\\n- **Sink:** T14 (CL3 handoff, aggregating T9/T12/T13a\\u2013c)\\n\\nKey flags surfaced in watch_items/meta_commentary: (1) the plan assumption's `default_combined_migrations()` **does not exist** \\u2014 executors must use `default_m6a_migrations()` + a CL2-built combined tuple passed to `SqliteLedgerMigrator(store, registry)` without editing `ledger_migrations.py`; (2) only `schemas.py`/`semantic_loop.py`/`__init__.py` are ported \\u2014 the other 5 archive files are cancelled-CL2 reference only; (3) the unaccepted-CL1-handoff assumption (5 blockers) must stay encoded so later gates can reject.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"task_contract_version\\\":2,\\\"validation_jobs\\\":[],\\\"critique_resolution_coverage\\\":[],\\\"tasks\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T1\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Port the CL1 critique_ledger module verbatim from the paused-epic archive and prove v1 byte-equivalent round-trip\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Copy the archived CL1 sources verbatim into the live tree: arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py, arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py, arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py from /workspace/.paused-epics/critique-ledger-m9-glm-20260723/Arnold/arnold/critique_ledger/. Do NOT port the 5 cancelled-CL2 files (cl2_migrations.py, ledger_writer.py, m6_importer.py, manifest_store.py, wbc_bridge.py) \\u2014 those are read-only reference, audited in T12. Create tests/arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py and tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py with a golden round-trip test: serialize every CL1 dataclass/enum via to_dict, deserialize via from_dict, assert byte-equivalent canonical JSON and matching canonical_hash for SELECTED/COMPLETED/FAILED/DROPPED/MALFORMED/TOMBSTONED/NO_ADDITIONAL_FINDINGS occurrences and all DispositionFamily/Relationship values. Confirm `import arnold.critique_ledger` succeeds and the __all__ exports match the archive __init__.py. Run the golden test.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py\\\",\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py\\\",\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Verbatim copy of 3 self-contained files is mechanical, but it establishes the module contract every downstream task depends on and the golden round-trip test must catch any silent copy/import error; a dropped export or wrong SCHEMA_VERSION constant cascades into all later tasks.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T2\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Add additive v2 schema versioning to schemas.py preserving v1 deserialization\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend schemas.py additively: add SCHEMA_VERSION_V2='cl.schema.v2' and CompatibilityProfile.V2_STRICT alongside the existing v1 constants (do not remove/rename v1). Add v2-only fields with defaults so v1 records still deserialize: supersedes_event_id (Optional[str]), region_anchors (tuple), tripwire_state (mapping) on the occurrence/reconciliation envelopes. Add new response/outcome/audit event dataclasses (RevisionResponseEvent, VerifiedOutcomeEvent, AuditDisagreementEvent, SupersedesReconciliationEvent) with to_dict/from_dict and canonical_hash. Enforce that v2 strict-mode occurrences REJECT semantic_finding_id on raw occurrences (raw occurrences never author semantic identity \\u2014 North Star invariant 16) while v1_preserve still accepts legacy records. Extend test_schemas_golden.py: v2 round-trip, v1-records-still-deserialize under v2 reader, strict-mode rejection assertion. Run the golden suite.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T1\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T1\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"v2 additions are layered onto the ported schemas.py and must not regress the v1 golden round-trip T1 established\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py ported from CL1 + passing test_schemas_golden.py\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":6,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Changes the schema contract the entire ledger depends on: new version constant, strict-mode rejection semantics, and four new event dataclasses with backward-compatible defaults that must keep v1 records deserializing \\u2014 a subtle field-default or strict-mode error passes simple tests but corrupts reconciliation, so it earns tier 6 not lower.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T3\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Make the pure semantic_loop functions v2-aware without changing v1 behavior\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Update semantic_loop.py pure functions (apply_disposition_events, apply_reconciliation_events, build_briefing, construct_manifest, project_gate_input, project_reviser_input, replay_full, validate_occurrence_custody) to accept and propagate v2 fields (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state) and the new response/outcome/audit/supersedes event types. Superseded reconciliation events must yield latest accepted decision state while retaining both original and superseding events (North Star invariant 5/15). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py: replay over a supersession chain resolves to the latest accepted decision; tripwire_state propagates into briefing/projection outputs; v1-only inputs still produce identical outputs to the ported v1 behavior. Run the semantic loop tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T1\\\",\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T1\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The loop functions live in the ported semantic_loop.py and must be extended in place\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py ported from CL1\\\"},\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The loop must handle the v2 fields and new event dataclasses T2 defines\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclasses (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, response/outcome/audit events)\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_semantic_loop.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":5,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Extends already-pure deterministic functions to thread v2 fields through reconciliation/briefing/projection and resolve supersession to latest-accepted state; the logic is well-understood but the supersession-resolution and tripwire-propagation paths are non-obvious enough to need deliberate care, placing it at tier 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T4\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Define CL2 domain DDL migrations as forward-fix-only registry versions 5+\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/cl2_migrations.py defining domain table DDL as Migration(version=5+...) entries with idempotent statements (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) for the cumulative occurrence, reconciliation-event, disposition-event, response/outcome/audit-event, manifest, and tripwire tables whose columns mirror the v2 schema fields. Add a combined-registry helper, e.g. default_cl2_migrations() returning default_m6a_migrations()+CL2_tuple (NOTE: the plan assumption names default_combined_migrations() which does not exist \\u2014 build the combination here; do NOT edit arnold/workflow/ledger_migrations.py per SD2). Verify SqliteLedgerMigrator(store, registry) applies versions 5+ idempotently, is crash-resume safe, and that editing an applied migration's statements raises MigrationChecksumMismatchError. Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py. Run the migration tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":13,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The DDL column set must mirror the v2 schema fields (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, response/outcome/audit events) T2 defines so stored rows round-trip\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclass field set\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/cl2_migrations.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":5,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Defines a new schema state-machine (versioned, checksum-validated, forward-fix-only migrations the migrator enforces) whose columns must exactly match the v2 dataclasses; an idempotency or checksum mistake silently corrupts crash-resume, earning tier 5.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T5\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the domain append layer with atomic occurrence+manifest+outbox commit in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/store.py with a CL2 domain store that shares the SQLite WAL connection with SqliteAttemptLedgerStore (same DB, separate class \\u2014 not a subclass, not a parallel authority). append_occurrence() writes occurrence + LedgerRevisionManifest + outbox entry atomically inside a single BEGIN IMMEDIATE via SqliteLedgerOutbox.append_event_with_outbox on the shared connection, so a simulated mid-tx crash leaves no partial accepted ledger revision. Enforce idempotency-key dedup (no double-insert), quarantine divergent duplicates, and single-terminal enforcement. Reuse (do not reimplement) the WBC substrate's WAL/isolation_level=None/busy-retry/_append_tx primitives and payload_policy InlinePayloadPolicy for inline/retention/redaction. Partial occurrences are evidence-only (ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED, cannot carry semantic_finding_id, cannot close \\u2014 SD4). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py: atomic commit, mid-tx-crash leaves no partial state, idempotency dedup, divergent-duplicate quarantine, partial-publication cannot expose incomplete revision. Run store append tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\",\\\"T4\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The store serializes v2 schema records into domain tables and must enforce PARTIAL_RECOVERED evidence-only semantics\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"schemas.py v2 dataclasses + ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED\\\"},\\\"T4\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The store appends to the domain tables created by T4's migrations and consumes the combined M6A+CL2 registry\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"cl2_migrations.py domain DDL + combined registry\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/store.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":true,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[\\\"completed_subobjectives\\\",\\\"remaining_subobjectives\\\",\\\"output_hashes\\\",\\\"test_state\\\"]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":8,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Major subsystem with genuine concurrency/transaction-semantics risk: atomic cross-table append on a shared WAL connection, idempotency-key dedup, single-terminal enforcement, divergent-duplicate quarantine, and outbox integration where a mid-tx-crash or dedup error silently corrupts ledger integrity \\u2014 mistakes here pass simple tests but break under contention, placing it at tier 8.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T6\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the read-only deterministic cumulative/domain projection and replay engine\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create arnold/critique_ledger/replay.py as a pure read-only module that reconstructs the cumulative finding set and per-domain projections by replaying stored events through the v2-aware semantic_loop functions. Replay must be deterministic (same inputs -> byte-identical cumulative projection across runs) and provably side-effect-free: no model call, no mutation, no external effect, no write to plan/gate/lifecycle/queue. It reads only committed rows and derives semantic finding identity, dispositions, and supersession (latest-accepted state while retaining both events). Add tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py: deterministic replay of a fixture event stream produces byte-identical output across two runs, read-only assertion (no store/gate/queue mutation), and supersession resolves to latest accepted. Run replay tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T3\\\",\\\"T5\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T3\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Replay drives stored events through the v2-aware semantic_loop functions T3 extended\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"semantic_loop.py v2-aware replay_full/apply_* functions\\\"},\\\"T5\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Replay reads the committed occurrence/manifest/event rows the store appends\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"store.py committed append interface + row schema\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/replay.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":true,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[\\\"completed_subobjectives\\\",\\\"remaining_subobjectives\\\",\\\"output_hashes\\\",\\\"test_state\\\"]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":7,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Demanding deterministic-engine work over a broad surface: byte-identical replay across runs, provable read-only/no-mutation guarantees, and correct supersession-to-latest-accepted resolution \\u2014 a non-determinism or side-effect bug is subtle and passes naive tests, earning tier 7.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T7\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the bounded active-action projection (must_act | must_revalidate | context_only)\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py (create it) with the active-action projection derived from T6 replay output. Expose must_act | must_revalidate | context_only per finding. Enforce: closed history does not grow must_act (active set stays bounded as history grows), unaudited non-action cannot remove a finding from the active set (North Star invariant 10), and batch actions enumerate every finding ID. Add active-action tests to tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py: closed finding moves out of must_act, unaudited non-action leaves it in, batch action covers all IDs, projection bounded as closed history grows. Run projection tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":13,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T6\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T6\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The active-action projection is derived from the cumulative replay output T6 produces\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"replay.py cumulative projection interface\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py\\\",\\\"tests/ar