u2192T5\\u2192T6\\u2192T7\\u2192T8\\u2192T13\\u2192T14, with T4 feeding T5, T10/T11 branching off T5 in parallel with the projections chain, and T12 (audit) as an independent leaf. All dependencies are correctness data dependencies (consumes_output/write_conflict) \\u2014 none for routing. Critique clearance had 0 findings so `critique_resolution_coverage` is `[]`.\\n\\n{\\\"task_contract_version\\\":2,\\\"tasks\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T1\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Port the CL1 critique_ledger module verbatim from the paused-epic archive and add v1 golden round-trip tests\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Copy schemas.py, semantic_loop.py, __init__.py from /workspace/.paused-epics/critique-ledger-m9-glm-20260723/Arnold/arnold/critique_ledger/ into arnold/critique_ledger/ (fix import paths). Create tests/arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py and test_schemas_golden.py proving every v1 dataclass round-trips byte-identically via to_dict/from_dict in strict and preserve modes, canonical_hash is stable, strict rejects unknown fields, preserve retains _extra. Confirm `from arnold.critique_ledger import CritiqueOccurrenceEnvelope, replay_full, canonical_hash` imports cleanly.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":10,\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py\\\",\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py\\\",\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Verbatim port of three pre-written files plus golden serialization tests; the port is mechanical and the module has no existing consumers yet, so blast radius is contained to byte-equivalence correctness of the round-trip and canonical_hash stability.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T2\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Add additive v2 schema versioning with new event dataclasses and strict-mode semantic-identity rejection\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In schemas.py add SCHEMA_VERSION_V2='cl.schema.v2', SUPPORTED_VERSIONS={v1,v2}, CompatibilityProfile.V2_STRICT/V2_PRESERVE, ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED. Make new v2 occurrences reject semantic_finding_id in strict mode (preserve keeps it as legacy_semantic_finding_id). Additively extend FindingReconciliationEvent with supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state (keep v1 defaults). Add FindingResponseEvent, OutcomeVerificationEvent, AuditEvent dataclasses (frozen, strict/preserve like existing). Extend __init__.py exports. Add v2 golden tests to test_schemas_golden.py: v2 occ rejects semantic_finding_id in strict; supersedes/response/outcome/audit round-trip; v1 records still deserialize.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T1\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T1\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"T2 additively versions schemas.py and extends __init__.py exports, both created by T1's port\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py and __init__.py ported verbatim from the CL1 archive\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/schemas.py\\\",\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/__init__.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Changes the schema contract every later task depends on; the v2 strict-mode rejection of semantic_finding_id (new occurrences cannot author semantic identity) and the additively-extended reconciliation/response/outcome/audit dataclasses carry subtle versioning invariants, and a defect here propagates silently through migrations, store, replay, and projections.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T3\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Make the semantic loop v2-aware: accept v2, resolve append-only supersession, enforce partial-occurrence evidence-only contract\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In semantic_loop.py relax the schema_version checks at lines ~1008 and ~1082 (schema_version != SCHEMA_VERSION) to accept both v1 and v2. Add supersession resolution: when a reconciliation carries supersedes_event_id, append the superseding decision and derive latest valid state (accepted|review_required|disputed|superseded) while retaining both events; superseded decisions do not support clean gate projection. Add partial-occurrence handling: occurrences with parse_status=PARTIAL_RECOVERED are evidence-only (no semantic_finding_id, cannot close a finding, missing fields unknown with unavailable_reason). Add v2 pure-loop tests to test_schemas_golden.py.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"v2 loop logic depends on v2 schema symbols: SUPPORTED_VERSIONS with v2, supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, ParseStatus.PARTIAL_RECOVERED\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"v2 schema constants, supersedes_event_id field, PARTIAL_RECOVERED enum, and v2 dataclasses in schemas.py\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/semantic_loop.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_schemas_golden.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Modifies the core reconciliation engine: append-only supersession resolution must derive latest decision state while never rewriting or discarding the original event, and the partial-occurrence evidence-only rule is a custody boundary, so subtle logic errors pass basic tests but corrupt finding history.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T4\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Define CL2 domain DDL migrations as versions 5+ appended to the M6A registry with idempotent forward-fix-only statements\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create cl2_migrations.py with cl2_domain_migrations() returning versions 5+ continuing default_m6a_migrations() (versions 1-4). All DDL IF NOT EXISTS / ADD COLUMN only, never DROP. Create tables: critique_occurrences, reconciliation_events, disposition_events, response_events, outcome_verification_events, audit_events, ledger_revision_manifests, region_freshness_state (each with monotonic sequence, event_id PK, idempotency_key, round_label, plus domain + v2 columns matching schemas.py). Add six indexes ((round_label,sequence), (semantic_finding_id), (attempt_id,occurrence_id), (canonical_finding_id), (region_anchor,finding_id), etc.). Provide default_combined_migrations()=default_m6a_migrations()+cl2_domain_migrations(). Do NOT edit ledger_migrations.py. Add test_cl2_migrations.py: idempotency (run twice is no-op), crash-resume, checksum guard rejects edited statements, no DROP.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T2\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T2\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"DDL column names must match the v2 schema fields (supersedes_event_id, region_anchors, tripwire_state, response/outcome/audit columns) defined by T2\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"v2 schema field set and column naming in schemas.py\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/cl2_migrations.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_cl2_migrations.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":3,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Additive DDL mirroring the proven default_m6a_migrations()/Migration pattern; the migrator and checksum machinery are reused unchanged. Surface is bounded to one new file; the real care is idempotent IF NOT EXISTS statements and contiguous version numbering 5+.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T5\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build CritiqueLedgerStore with atomic append-domain-tx, typed append methods, and outbox crash recovery on the shared SQLite connection\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create store.py: CritiqueLedgerStore over a shared SqliteAttemptLedgerStore connection (same DB/WAL), runs default_combined_migrations() via SqliteLedgerMigrator on first open. Implement _append_domain_tx mirroring _append_tx: BEGIN IMMEDIATE busy-retry, then idempotency-key dedup (dedup wins, divergent quarantined), post-terminal rejection, monotonic sequence, INSERT domain event, revision manifest upsert, outbox record, COMMIT (one transaction, all-or-nothing). Typed methods: append_occurrence, append_reconciliation (supersession), append_disposition, append_response, append_outcome_verification, append_audit, finalize_revision (publishes LedgerRevisionManifest only after complete occurrence accounting; no partial publication), record_attempt_start (must succeed before dispatch; terminal failure surfaces persistence_failed|indeterminate). Use SqliteLedgerOutbox.append_event_with_outbox pattern. Add test_store_append.py: append atomicity + simulated mid-tx crash leaves no partial state, idempotency dedup prevents double-insert, divergent duplicates quarantined, partial publication blocked, supersession appends without rewriting original, outbox get_stale_pending+retry_failed recover crashed writes.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":15,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T3\\\",\\\"T4\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T3\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"store serializes/deserializes domain events through the v2-aware dataclasses and supersession handling from T3\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"v2-aware semantic_loop and v2 dataclasses\\\"},\\\"T4\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"store writes to the domain tables created by T4's migrations via default_combined_migrations()\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"cl2_domain_migrations() + default_combined_migrations() registry and domain DDL tables\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/store.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_store_append.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":6,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"The new persistence authority for the ledger: atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE cross-table writes, idempotency-key dedup with divergent quarantine, post-terminal enforcement, and outbox crash recovery all on the shared WAL connection. Difficulty is bounded by mirroring the proven _append_tx/append_event_with_outbox patterns, but a subtle atomicity or idempotency error passes unit tests while corrupting custody, so elevated blast radius justifies tier 6.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T6\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build read-only deterministic replay that scans domain tables and reconstructs cumulative projections with stable hashes\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create replay.py: replay_projections(store)->ReplayResult scans all domain event tables ordered by (round_label, sequence), reconstructs typed dataclass lists, and calls the pure semantic_loop replay_full-family functions. Replay writes NOTHING: no INSERT/UPDATE, no model call, no external effect; assert no new rows and no file mutations. ReplayResult carries deterministic SHA-256 hashes of canonical serialized projections for byte-equivalence checks across runs. Add test_replay.py: replay determinism (same inputs byte-identical across two runs), duplicate replay no-op, replay mutates nothing, and the M6 blocked-handoff family reconstructs as one finding with five retained occurrences while the accepted replay limitation retains its disposition.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T5\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T5\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"replay scans domain event tables via the CritiqueLedgerStore read API implemented by T5\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"CritiqueLedgerStore with queryable domain event tables\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/replay.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_replay.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"Deterministic, provably side-effect-free replay is a subtle correctness contract: the read-only/no-mutation guarantee and byte-stable hashes must hold while correctly reconstructing the M6 five-occurrence family. The pure replay functions already exist (T3), bounding difficulty to the read-path wiring and invariants.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T7\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the active-action projection with bounded must_act/must_revalidate/context_only queues and audit-gated removal\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create projections.py: build_active_action_projection(events)->ActiveActionView deriving three bounded queues: must_act (open action-required findings), must_revalidate (stale/tripwire-triggered needing re-reconciliation), context_only (closed/superseded/accepted-risk, visible but not actionable). Guarantee boundedness: closed history does not grow must_act/must_revalidate; dispositions removing a finding from the active set require risk-based non-zero audit; boilerplate or unaudited non-action cannot remove a finding; batch actions enumerate every finding ID. Create test_projections.py with active-action tests.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T6\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T6\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"consumes_output\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"the active-action projection consumes the replay-sorted event stream / ReplayResult produced by T6\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"replay_projections() and ReplayResult with sorted events\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"The boundedness and audit-gate invariants are subtle correctness rules that gate consumption: unaudited non-action must stay in must_act and closed history must not grow the active queues. Bounded to one new file, but an error here lets stale closure or boilerplate non-action suppress real findings.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T8\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Build the per-round accountability projection mapping attempt to occurrence to finding to response to verified outcome to reopen\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Extend projections.py with build_round_accountability(events)->tuple[RoundReceipt,...] mapping the full chain per round: critic attempt, occurrence, logical finding/reconciliation, response/non-action, verified outcome, reopen condition. Account for EVERY parseable occurrence and active finding. Keep reviser 'addressed' (FindingResponseEvent) distinct from independently verified dealt_with|partially_dealt_with|not_dealt_with|unknown (OutcomeVerificationEvent); a receipt with no outcome verification shows unknown. Add round-accountability tests to test_projections.py: every occurrence/finding accounted for, addressed!=verified, missing verification=unknown, the five-occurrence M6 family yields one receipt with five occurrence rows.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":12,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T7\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T7\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"write_conflict\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"T8 extends projections.py and test_projections.py created by T7 with the round-accountability projection\\\",\\\"required_output\\\":\\\"projections.py with ActiveActionView and test_projections.py with active-action tests\\\"}},\\\"routing_group\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"write_set\\\":{\\\"paths\\\":[\\\"arnold/critique_ledger/projections.py\\\",\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"complete\\\":true},\\\"narrow_tests\\\":{\\\"selectors\\\":[\\\"tests/arnold/critique_ledger/test_projections.py\\\"],\\\"max_seconds\\\":120,\\\"max_runs\\\":2},\\\"checkpoint\\\":{\\\"required\\\":false,\\\"max_interval_seconds\\\":300,\\\"records\\\":[]},\\\"status\\\":\\\"pending\\\",\\\"executor_notes\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reviewer_verdict\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"complexity\\\":4,\\\"complexity_justification\\\":\\\"The per-round chain mapping with the addressed!=verified-outcome distinction and the account-for-every-occurrence/finding completeness rule is subtle; an error conflates the reviser's self-claim with independent verification, which is exactly the accountability failure the ledger exists to prevent.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"T9\\\",\\\"objective\\\":\\\"Add correction/supersession, audit-disagreement, and deterministic-tripwire replay tests through the append-to-projection path\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Add fixtures to test_projections.py exercising v2 event types through append->replay->projection: (1) correction/supersession: append a superseding reconciliation, replay derives latest decision retaining both, superseded decision does not support clean gate projection; (2) audit disagreement: append AuditEvent decision=disputed, audit failure cannot silently preserve closure, disputed status visible and actionable in the active projection; (3) tripwire determinism: deterministic tripwire fires on region/evidence/dependency change, near-match, audit disagreement, or stale model/schema revision; tripwire triggers needs_reconciliation in must_revalidate, never semantic merge/closure/suppression.\\\",\\\"estimated_minutes\\\":10,\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"T8\\\"],\\\"dependency_reasons\\\":{\\\"T8\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"write_conflict\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"T9 adds correction/audit/tripwire fixtures to test_projections.py e